  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pastoral da Aids- Engaging the Catholic Church in the Fight against HIV and Aids</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to combating the AIDS epidemic through building the capacity of pastoral agents to undertake prevention interventions and education that reduce the level of new infections, to provide care and accompaniment of people living with HIV and AIDS (PLWHAs), and to play an active role in influencing policy on HIV and AIDS in Brazil and improve access to public services and social rights.

Officially created in 2002, Pastoral da AIDS is a service organisation affiliated to the Brazilian Bishops Conference of the Catholic Church. Its aim is the reduction of the HIV and AIDS epidemic by engaging the local community in the struggle. Its chief areas of activity are: prevention, advocacy and campaigning, capacity strengthening, counselling, accompaniment and care of PLWHAs.

Pastoral da AIDS works on two levels: ensuring a consistent proactive response to the epidemic from the Church leadership and involving the broader communities fully in their work. It has its roots in voluntary work and relies upon this strong network of volunteers who work within the structures of the Catholic Church. At present, 3,000 volunteers working in 75 dioceses are engaged in capacity strengthening activities in the areas of preventive education, accompaniment of people living with HIV and AIDS and social accountability. More than 20,000 people living with HIV and AIDS are indirectly being benefited from home and hospital visits, and care and accompaniment by drop in and support centres linked to Pastoral da AIDS.</narrative>
  </description>
